    {
      "id": "b1f047f3-0378-4284-a771-67a3234eb363",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Come up with a story hook. What is the value that your readers will get from reading your post? Yes, I’m asking you to write a click-baity title. “Learn The Secrets Of Quantum By Playing Tetris!”, “CookAlong: Unlock Your Inner Chef”. These titles offer something to the reader, a reward, knowledge, and quick fun read.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "8bb33203-6d86-4681-88f1-c7ddb912fb73",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use Medium as ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.hubspot.com/inbound-marketing",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "inbound marketing",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". You offer content that has some intrinsic value (the article), at the same time drawing readers in to learn more about your project and want to download it, use it, etc.  Don’t write about your project as a class project, that won’t draw many viewers, instead, write about it as if you were a startup and wanted to draw people in.  Tease them with the problem you are solving or some technological innovation or even some workaround you had to do.  ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
